        "answer": {
          "short": "For example, $(2\\times3)^2=2^2\\times3^2=36$; $(4\\times5)^2=4^2\\times5^2=400$; $(5\\times6)^2=5^2\\times6^2=900$.",
          "worked": "For example:\n$$\\begin{align*}(2\\times3)^2 &= 6^2=36\\\\2^2\\times3^2 &= 4\\times9=36\\\\(4\\times5)^2 &= 20^2=400\\\\4^2\\times5^2 &= 16\\times25=400\\\\(5\\times6)^2 &= 30^2=900\\\\5^2\\times6^2 &= 25\\times36=900\\end{align*}$$\nThe two sides agree for each pair. These examples illustrate the rule; checking examples alone does not prove it for all numbers.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 45
      }
